[TEXT] === DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: dswa1, dswa2
diagnosis_text:
Affected component: the VRRP gateway for Office A (keepalived on VLAN 10) running on the distribution switches dswa1/dswa2. Mechanism: Both switches are configured with an abnormally large VRRP advertisement interval (advert_int 4). With VRRP, the Master-Down timer is roughly 3 × advert_int plus a small skew, so a missed burst of adverts or a brief control-plane hiccup causes the BACKUP to wait ~12–13 seconds before taking over. During that window, the virtual IP 10.1.0.1 may not answer, which appears as the “gateway dies for a few seconds” the users observe every few minutes whenever there’s a transient (STP/OSPF churn or brief keepalived scheduling delay). Localization and evidence: On dswa1, br0.10 holds 10.
[FINAL] stop=no-more-tool-calls tool_calls=36
